<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n101608" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφᾰλερός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφάλλω</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>likely to make one
			stumble</i> or <i>trip</i> metaph., <i>slippery, perilous</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυραννὶς χρῆμα ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.53
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γνωμέω</span>
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">. . τὴν -ωτέρην σεωυτῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					7.16
				</span></i>
			.
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά; σφαλερὸν ἡγεμὼν θρασύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					508
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦτο δέ γ́ ἐστὶν τὸ καλὸν
			ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>IA</u>
				21
			</span></i> (anap.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ βιοτή . . ἐπὶ παντὶ σφαλερὰ κεῖσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					916
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάντων -ώτατον</span>, of
			future events, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.62
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				1.1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτατοι καιροί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Oec.</u>
					p.48
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">J.,
				<u>SIG</u>796</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>B</u>
				10
			</span></i> (Epid., <span class="entity">i A.D.</span>); of poems, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				810b
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. τρόπος</span> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόπος</span>
			) <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Prog.</u>
				22
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφαλερόν [ἐστι</span>], c.
				inf., <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				451a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lg.</u>
				688b
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἐπιχειρῆσαι ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				2.1.2
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				Comp.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερον, νοσεῖν</span> to be <i>more
				dangerously</i> ill, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				15.724
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφάλλομαι</span>) <i>ready to fall, tottering,
				reeling</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					371
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥῦμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					159
				</span></i>
			 (anap.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῶμα ς. ἐν ταῖς
			κινήσεσι</span>, of revellers and sufferers from coma, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				7.645
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕξις ς. πρὸς ὑγίειαν</span>
			<i>uncertain</i> in point of health, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				404a
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ρῶς, ὑγιαίνειν</span> enjoy health
				<i>precariously</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				6.810
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> of
			persons, where the sense often fluctuates between <i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴχνεσι σφαλεροί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Al.</u>
					189
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				400
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. σύμμαχοι</span>
			<i>uncertain</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				1.7
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προστάτης ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				774.3
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ρῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>IA</u>
					600
				</span></i>
			 (anap.), <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				7.1
			</span></i>.</div>
